# CortexWatt API (FastAPI) — production environment
#
# Copy to `.env` at the REPO ROOT on the server. app/config.py resolves
# Path(__file__).parents[3], i.e. <repo>/.env — not apps/api/.env.
#
#     cp .env.production.example .env && nano .env
#
# Real environment variables win over this file (pydantic-settings precedence),
# so anything exported by PM2 or the shell overrides what's written here.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MySQL — TWO DSNs, both required
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The async one (aiomysql) serves requests; the sync one (pymysql) is what
# Alembic runs migrations through. Set only one and `alembic upgrade head`
# fails on deploy while the app itself looks fine.
#
# Port: Cloudways MySQL is 3306. The 8889 in local dev is MAMP-only.
#
# ⚠ URL-ENCODE the password.
#
#   The one that will actually bite you is @. SQLAlchemy splits on the LAST
#   @, so a password of "p@ssword" yields host="ssword@127.0.0.1" with NO
#   error raised — you get a DNS/connection failure pointing at a hostname
#   you never typed. Verified against this project's SQLAlchemy version.
#
#   ! : / # parse fine in the password position here, unlike holigrowth's
#   Node/drizzle DSN where ! had to become %21 — different parser, stricter
#   rules. Don't assume the two behave the same.
#
#   Simplest safe policy: encode everything non-alphanumeric anyway. It is
#   never wrong, and the same string may later be pasted into a tool with a
#   stricter parser.
#     @ → %40    ! → %21    # → %23    : → %3A
#     / → %2F    ? → %3F    & → %26    % → %25
#
#   Encode with:
#     python3 -c "import urllib.parse,sys;print(urllib.parse.quote(sys.argv[1],safe=''))" 'yourpassword'
#
#   Verify the DSN parses to what you meant BEFORE deploying:
#     python3 -c "from sqlalchemy.engine import make_url;u=make_url('PASTE_DSN');print(u.host,u.port,u.database)"
#
# Cloudways gives you the DB name / user / password under
# Application Settings → Access Details.

DATABASE_URL=mysql+aiomysql://DB_USER:URL_ENCODED_PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:3306/DB_NAME
DATABASE_URL_SYNC=mysql+pymysql://DB_USER:URL_ENCODED_PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:3306/DB_NAME

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Redis — REQUIRED, not optional
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not just leaderboards: POST /v1/sessions calls check_rate_limit() first,
# which INCRs a Redis key. There is no fallback path — if Redis is unreachable,
# nobody can start a game. Treat it as a hard dependency, same tier as MySQL.
#
# Install it on Cloudways under
#   Server Management → Settings & Packages → Packages → Redis
# It then listens on 127.0.0.1:6379.
#
# Use a DEDICATED DB INDEX. Other apps share this VM (colorgifts, holigrowth),
# and index 0 is the default everything else grabs. /1 keeps `lb:*` and `rl:*`
# keys isolated, and lets you FLUSHDB this app without touching the others.

REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379/1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets — generate fresh, never reuse the dev values
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two DIFFERENT secrets. JWT_SECRET signs the login token; SESSION_TOKEN_SECRET
# signs the per-session HMAC that makes results tamper-evident (PRD §3). Reusing
# one value for both means a leaked login token also forges session results.
#
#     openssl rand -hex 32     # run twice, paste one into each
#
# Rotating JWT_SECRET logs everyone out. Rotating SESSION_TOKEN_SECRET
# invalidates any session issued but not yet submitted (15-minute window).

JWT_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_openssl_rand_hex_32
SESSION_TOKEN_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_DIFFERENT_openssl_rand_hex_32

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CORS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The single browser origin allowed to call this API. Exact scheme + host,
# NO trailing slash, NO wildcard.
#
# With the recommended same-origin setup (Apache proxies ^/v1/ on
# app.cortexwatt.com through to uvicorn) the browser never makes a
# cross-origin request, so this is belt-and-braces. It still matters if you
# later split the API onto its own subdomain.

WEB_ORIGIN=https://app.cortexwatt.com

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional tunables — defaults in app/config.py, override only if needed
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SESSION_TTL_MINUTES=15        # how long an issued session stays submittable
# SESSION_ISSUES_PER_HOUR=30    # per-user rate limit on POST /v1/sessions
